assertion  XSH.towlower.001
anchor     functions/towlower.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/towlower.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale towlower() maps each of the 26 uppercase
           letters to the corresponding lowercase letter.
test       t/001-mapping.c

assertion  XSH.towlower.002
anchor     functions/towlower.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/towlower.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       towlower() returns the other portable characters unchanged: the
           lowercase letters, the digits, the punctuation, the space and the
           control characters.
test       t/002-unchanged.c

assertion  XSH.towlower.003
anchor     functions/towlower.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/towlower.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       towlower(WEOF) returns WEOF (an argument of the domain with no
           mapping is returned unchanged).
test       t/003-weof.c

assertion  XSH.towlower.004
anchor     functions/towlower.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/towlower.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       For each uppercase letter c, towupper(towlower(c)) equals c and the
           result of towlower(c) is a lowercase letter in the class sense
           (iswupper or iswlower as appropriate).
test       t/004-round-trip.c
